OL,3,AHong Kong's Tiananmen activists
OL,4,Asentenced to up to seven years in
OL,5,Aprison
OL,6,
OL,7,FThree Hong Kong activists who organised
OL,8,Fannual vigils commemorating Beijing's
OL,9,F1989 crackdown on Tiananmen Square
OL,10,Fprotests have been handed prison
OL,11,Fsentences of up to seven years.
OL,13,FLee Cheuk-yan, 69, and Chow Hang-tung,
OL,14,F41, were convicted last month of
OL,15,Finciting others to subvert state power,
OL,16,Funder the city's controversial national
OL,17,Fsecurity law. A third defendant, Albert
OL,18,FHo, 74, had pleaded guilty in January.
OL,20,FThe office of United Nations human
OL,21,Frights chief Volker Turk called for
OL,22,F"these sentences to be quashed".
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
